its own, or a lab (under `labs/`) or workshop (under `workshops/`) etc.  I hope it makes some sense ;-)\nIn your \"superdataset\" you could have your \"brains/\" if you really like, but indeed it might be hard to \"identify\" such a dataset, although it might be an appropriate name for some subdataset with a study, along with other subdatasets such as \"intestines/\" and \"undefined/\" ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1536905128,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTI0MTA0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2826#issuecomment-421241049"},"message":"\u003e What determines the naming of the superdataset?\n\n@yarikoptic does. ;-) (for http://datasets.datalad.org)\n\nThis is a collection of datasets maintained by him, hence he makes the decisions. Not just regarding the names of superdatasets, but also regarding the levels of nesting etc. A different maintainer of a different collection can easily go for a different model. Your dataset, your choice.\n\nThere is one special aspect here, as http://datasets.datalad.org is not just a re-mix of datasets presented in a specific view, but in fact the actual origin of many of its datasets (but not for all of them). However, that does not change the fact that each dataset in this collection is its own entity, and it would probably be less then an hour to create a new superdataset that has all datasets from http://datasets.datalad.org re-mixed in a different way (e.g. a flat list) and post that on github.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1536905139,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE4NDUyNzExNTM="},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"3286e9a6aeeb25e1bf3fcf613be9da3d3270e55d"},"timestamp":1536930783,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMTM1NDA2OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2826#issuecomment-421354069"},"message":"Ah ok, understood, all hail @yarikoptic master of the data! This is something that is good to know that I'll think about as I develop stuffs. I think likely a strategy we can somewhat hope for is that the organization and naming doesn't matter **so** much because the metadata and search of it can provide the discoverability that a user needs.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"3286e9a6aeeb25e1bf3fcf613be9da3d3270e55d"},"timestamp":1536930783,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTg0NjA3NzA1MQ=="},"status":2}]}